---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'About Marc Evans | US Gravity';
const description = 'Stratospheric thinking. Ground-level execution. Meet Marc Evans — the Virtual CIO and IT consulting expert behind Gravity Limited. Based in Denver, CO, serving companies across the USA.';
const permalink = `${Astro.site.href}about`;
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} permalink={permalink} current="about">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="about-header">
      <div class="about-text-lead">
        <p class="eyebrow">Stratospheric Thinking. Ground-Level Execution.</p>
        <h1>Your Technology Has Been in Freefall. Let's Change That.</h1>
        <!-- Freefall accent SVG -->
        <svg class="freefall-accent" viewBox="0 0 320 48" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
          <!-- Ground baseline -->
          <line x1="0" y1="44" x2="320" y2="44" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.15"/>
          <!-- Freefall arc — object dropping and landing -->
          <path d="M40,4 C80,-2 160,8 200,44" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 3" opacity="0.3"/>
          <!-- Landing node -->
          <circle cx="200" cy="44" r="4" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.5"/>
          <!-- Ripple rings at landing -->
          <circle cx="200" cy="44" r="10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.18"/>
          <circle cx="200" cy="44" r="18" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5" opacity="0.1"/>
          <!-- Origin dot -->
          <circle cx="40" cy="4" r="2.5" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.3"/>
          <!-- Small stars -->
          <circle cx="260" cy="12" r="1.2" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.2"/>
          <circle cx="290" cy="28" r="1"   fill="currentColor" opacity="0.15"/>
          <circle cx="16"  cy="20" r="1"   fill="currentColor" opacity="0.15"/>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="about-body">
      <figure class="about-image">
        <div class="portrait-wrap">
          <img src="/assets/marc-evans.jpg" alt="Marc Evans, Founder of Gravity Limited" class="portrait-photo"/>
          <div class="portrait-caption">
            <p class="portrait-name">Marc Evans</p>
            <p class="portrait-title">Founder &amp; Virtual CIO</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>

      <div class="about-content">
        <h2>Hi, I'm Marc Evans.</h2>

        <p>
          I'm a Virtual CIO and IT strategy consultant based in Denver, Colorado, working with companies across the United States. I align technology with where the business is actually going — without the cost of a full-time CIO hire.
        </p>

        <p>
          Most small and mid-size companies don't need a CIO 40 hours a week. They need that level of thinking on the decisions that matter — the vendor selections, the strategic roadmap, the board-level conversation about technology risk. That's where I plug in.
        </p>

        <h2>What I Actually Do</h2>

        <p>
          I scale to fit what your business actually needs — using the team and tools you already have.
        </p>

        <p>
          Sometimes that means working alongside a strong IT Manager who needs an executive partner for strategy, vendor selection, or board conversations — making them more effective, not replacing them. Sometimes it means coaching and developing an IT team into the high-performing function the business actually requires. Sometimes it means managing the relationship with your MSP or MSSP so you're getting full value for what you're paying. And sometimes it means filling a strategic gap until you're ready to hire a full-time IT executive.
        </p>

        <p>
          My job is to make your IT operation more <strong>aligned</strong>, more <strong>accountable</strong>, and more <strong>valuable to the business</strong> — without the overhead of another executive on payroll.
        </p>

        <h2>Selected Track Record</h2>

        <p>
          A few representative things I've delivered over my career:
        </p>

        <ul class="track-record">
          <li><strong>OT systems running inside nuclear reactors</strong> — designed and built operational technology solutions deployed in active nuclear facilities, where reliability and regulatory rigor aren't optional.</li>
          <li><strong>Statewide AV platform for Colorado courts</strong> — created the audio/visual solution that became the standard for the Colorado State Judicial system and was adopted by several surrounding states.</li>
          <li><strong>IT team turnarounds</strong> — repeatedly taken underperforming IT teams and turned them into the high-performing function the business actually needed, without replacing the people in seat.</li>
          <li><strong>Compliance automation</strong> — helped companies automate the documentation, evidence collection, and controls that keep them audit-ready — across CMMC, SOC 2, HIPAA, and industry-specific frameworks.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          This experience shapes how I think, what risks I look for, and what's actually achievable in your environment.
        </p>

        <h2>Industries I Know Well</h2>

        <p>
          I've built deep experience in industries where technology failures aren't just costly — they're consequential. That includes Energy, Mining and Prospecting, Power Generation, and Industrial and BioMedical Manufacturing — environments where uptime matters, compliance is non-negotiable, and the margin for error is thin.
        </p>

        <p>
          Just as often, I work with the businesses that supply and serve those industries — the engineering firms, specialized vendors, and B2B service providers whose own operations have to meet the same standards as their customers.
        </p>

        <p>
          That said, I've helped plenty of companies outside these sectors too. If your business is hitting a wall — scaling too fast, struggling with compliance, inheriting bad infrastructure, or simply lacking IT leadership — I can likely help.
        </p>

        <h2>Why "Gravity"?</h2>

        <p>
          Most IT problems aren't technical problems — they're alignment problems. Technology drifts away from the business. Decisions get made reactively. Vendors set the agenda. Teams optimize for their own goals instead of yours.
        </p>

        <p>
          Gravity is what holds it together — the strategic pull that keeps technology aligned with business goals, keeps vendors honest, keeps teams pointed in the same direction, and keeps the right decisions getting made even when the day-to-day pulls toward something easier.
        </p>

        <p>
          The tagline — <em>Stratospheric thinking. Ground-level execution.</em> — is the job. The long view and the actual delivery, from one person who's accountable for both.
        </p>

        <div class="about-cta">
          <p>Ready to have a real conversation about your IT situation?</p>
          <a href="mailto:usgravity.ethically151@passfwd.com" class="btn btn-primary">Reach Out to Marc</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-header {
    margin: 2em 0 2.5em;
    color: var(--text-link);
  }

  .freefall-accent {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 360px;
    height: 48px;
    margin-top: 1.2em;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.85em;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 0.4em;
  }

  .about-text-lead h1 {
    font-size: 2.2em;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.25;
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* ── Layout ── */
  .about-body {
    display: flex;
    gap: 3em;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .about-image {
    flex: 0 0 260px;
    margin: 0;
    position: sticky;
    top: 2em;
  }

  .about-content {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  /* ── Portrait ── */
  .portrait-wrap {
    position: relative;
    width: 240px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
  }

  .portrait-photo {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .portrait-caption {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
    padding: 0.6em 1em 0.75em;
    text-align: center;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .portrait-name {
    font-size: 0.95em;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 0.2em;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .portrait-title {
    font-size: 0.78em;
    opacity: 0.85;
    margin: 0;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  /* ── Content ── */
  .about-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.4em;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 1.8em 0 0.5em;
  }

  .about-content h2:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .about-content p {
    font-size: 1.05em;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1em;
    color: var(--text-main);
  }

  .about-content strong {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .track-record {
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    margin: 0.5em 0 1.5em;
  }

  .track-record li {
    margin-bottom: 0.9em;
    font-size: 1.02em;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-main);
  }

  /* ── CTA ── */
  .about-cta {
    margin-top: 2.5em;
    padding: 2em;
    background: var(--background-body-alt, #f6f8fc);
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .about-cta p {
    font-size: 1.1em;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 1em;
    color: var(--text-main);
  }

  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.75em 1.75em;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1em;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .btn:hover {
    opacity: 0.85;
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--text-link);
    color: #fff;
  }

  /* ── Responsive ── */
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .about-body {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .about-image {
      position: static;
      flex: none;
    }

    .about-text-lead h1 {
      font-size: 1.7em;
    }
  }
</style>
